Author: Eshan I. <79593316+eshankiyer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Tue Aug 4 10:34:12 2026 -0400

    fix(block): drop experience when a mob spawner is broken
    
    Vanilla's SpawnerBlock#spawnAfterBreak (net/minecraft/world/level/block/SpawnerBlock.java)
    rolls `15 + random.nextInt(15) + random.nextInt(15)` (range 15-43 inclusive) and pops it
    as experience orbs on every player break. The spawner's override does not route through
    Block#tryDropExperience/EnchantmentHelper#processBlockExperience the way ore blocks
    (DropExperienceBlock) do, and dropResources always calls spawnAfterBreak with
    dropExperience=true regardless of the tool used (Block.java dropResources overloads) -
    so Silk Touch does not suppress this drop, it only prevents obtaining the spawner block
    itself, which was already the case here since spawner has no loot table drop wired up.
    
    Pumpkin's SpawnerBlock had no `broken` hook at all, so breaking a spawner dropped no XP.
    Wire it up reusing the existing ExperienceOrbEntity::spawn helper (same one used by
    furnace/blast_furnace/smoker/hopper), with a pure spawner_break_experience() helper and
    a range unit test.

